# <Story title> — database schema

<N> table(s) added to / changed in `data/portfolio/portfolio.sqlite` (single shared DB via
`src/db.py`).
All Decimal fields stored as `TEXT`, read back via `Decimal(row["col"])`.
All timestamps stored as UTC ISO strings.
Created by `<StoreClass>.init_db()` — idempotent `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`; there is no
migration-file mechanism.

---

```sql
-- <one-line purpose>. Written by <writer>; read by <readers>.
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS <table_name> (
    <col>            TEXT PRIMARY KEY,     -- <meaning / format>
    <col>            TEXT NOT NULL,        -- Decimal as TEXT
    <col>            REAL,                 -- NULL when <condition>
    created_at       TEXT NOT NULL,        -- UTC ISO, when the row was written
    UNIQUE (<grain columns>)
);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_<table>_<cols>
    ON <table_name> (<cols>);
```

